## What the work does

Commit `4c48a8b12` adds the e2e, the hero unit case, and both workflow wirings.
Commit `b09e21f32` fixes the covered photo, the Tutor section, the squeezed portraits, and the home hero.
Two later commits record evidence. Tests were committed before the Green fix.

## What I verified

1. e2e meaning (AC-1). 56 cases cover 6 pages, 4 widths, 2 locales, plus 8 product-block cases.
   Missing hero, card, block, and Tutor photos each push a problem, so no check passes on a missing
   deliverable. Coverage walks a 5 x 5 `elementFromPoint` grid with `pointer-events` forced, scrolls
   per row, waits for load, and reports `measured==0` as an error.
   A text box can never count as the wrapper, because a wrapper must contain the img, hold no text,
   and hold one img.
2. Missing-deliverable fixtures. `playwright test e2e/no-such-file.spec.ts` printed
   `Error: No tests found.` and exited 1. The full suite with no server failed 56 tests and
   exited 1. A dead server and a missing spec both fail the gate.
3. CI and CD wiring (AC-3). In `ci.yml`, the Chrome install, `next start -p 3123` with a 60 x 2 s
   port wait, and the e2e all carry `if: matrix.id == 'www-reading-advantage'` and run after the
   build. In `cd-www-reading-advantage.yml`, no deploy step sits before the e2e; auth, gcloud, and
   Submit Cloud Build follow it, so a failing e2e stops the deploy.
   `cd-www-reading-advantage.yml` is the only www deploy path, because `cd-apps.yml` excludes
   `www-reading-advantage`.
   The Chrome install and the `pnpm --filter ... exec` form match `capture-real-logos.yml`.
   The background server does not block the job.
4. Red and Green evidence. `/tmp/opencode/a62-head-e2e2.log` line 624 reads `18 failed`, `38 passed`,
   which matches the Red claim. The gate log reads `56 passed` and `EXIT=0`. The checks log reads
   19 files and 323 tests with `EXIT=0`, `TSC=0`, `ESLINT=0`. Plan claims match these exits (A5).
5. AC-4 fixes. The report-results card now places the photo above the text with no overlay.
   The Tutor section shows `tutor-flashcard.webp` through `ProductPicture`, with `imageAlt` in en,
   th, and zh. Portrait pictures use `h-auto w-full max-w-48`.
   The home Mastery card sits under the photo below `lg` and overlaps a corner from `lg`.
6. Tutor set rules. The source file is `student-mobile/22-live-p02-flashcards.png`. It is not a
   price screen, not an admin screen, shows no stats strip, no faces, and no dev class names.
   It obeys the README use rules.
7. Regressions. `hero-section.tsx` does not change in this diff. `ProductPicture` is used only on
   `/products`. The home page change is local to that page.
   I ran `vitest run src/components/marketing/hero-section.test.tsx --maxWorkers=1` (7 passed),
   `vitest run src/__tests__/products-page-pictures.red.test.tsx --maxWorkers=1` (19 passed),
   `tsc --noEmit` (0), and `eslint` on the six touched files (0).

## Findings

- F1 (medium, nonblocking). The AC-1 aspect and short-side assertion skips two product pictures.
  `photos.spec.ts:590-613` keeps only photos with a `program-card-*` or `product-block-*` ancestor.
  The Tutor picture (`tutor-advantage.tsx:71-76`) and the report-results picture
  (`b2b-solutions.tsx:351-358`) have no such ancestor. A future squeeze of the Tutor picture would
  pass the gate. Both use ratio-preserving `h-auto w-full` today, and the same portrait class is
  aspect-checked in the three program cards. Fix by adding a testid or by extending the loop to
  `/images/products/` sources.
- F2 (low, nonblocking). The exclusion code skips two extra cases. `photos.spec.ts:147` skips an
  empty `src`, and `photos.spec.ts:155` skips a path segment that starts with `qr`, `logo`, or
  `icon`. A real photo named `icon-guide.png` would escape every check. Spec AC-1 allows only the
  listed rules.
- F3 (low, nonblocking). Plan task 1.1 keeps a stale proof line. The checked-off text claims a
  failing run at `8193625ca^` for hero and product photos, while the body of the same task says the
  pre-fix e2e was skipped. The Red evidence at HEAD is real, and the hero unit test fails at
  `8193625ca^`.

## Accepted deviation

The "See How We Report Results" card stays stacked at every width. Spec AC-4 asked for a
side-by-side layout from `lg`. The grid is `md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`
(`b2b-solutions.tsx:216`), so the cell is one third wide at `lg`, and a side-by-side layout would
shrink the photo. The stacked card keeps text off the photo, which is the owner complaint. The plan
records the deviation. I accept it.

